From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] cellFiber: PPU fiber contexts (cellFiberPpuContext*) on a host thread each

Upstream: not yet submitted; written to be upstreamed (generic, no title names)
Licence: MIT, as ps3recomp (see its LICENSE); offered under the same terms
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0010)

What: the SDK's low-level PPU fiber contexts, which had no handler (their
imports took the unresolved path and faked CELL_OK, so no context ever ran):
_cellFiberPpuContextAttributeInitialize, cellFiberPpuContextInitialize,
cellFiberPpuContextFinalize, cellFiberPpuContextRun, cellFiberPpuContextSwitch,
cellFiberPpuContextReturnToThread, cellFiberPpuContextSelf and
cellFiberPpuContextCheckStackLimit, in libs/spurs/cellFiber.c (so
gen_hle_nids.py registers them). A PPU thread runs a context with Run until a
context returns to the thread (Run then hands back its cause and the context);
contexts hand control to each other with Switch.

A lifted context's suspended state includes host frames (the lifted calls it
is inside), so each context runs on a host thread of its own, created by
Initialize, and a baton (one lock, a condition variable per context and per
Run) lets exactly one context, or the thread blocked in Run, execute at a
time. Unlike ucontext (which the scheduler API in the same file uses), this
keeps every host thread-local of the runtime per context without a list to
swap: the guest setjmp chain of ppu_sjlj.h (a guest longjmp can only reach a
setjmp made on its own context, and a context's chain starts empty), the
indirect-call depth, the tail-call trampoline, the callback stack slot. A
round trip costs about 5 us on an M4 Max.

Guest identity: a context runs on the PPU thread that resumed it, as on the
console, so each Run or Switch gives it that thread's thread_id and r13 (TLS).
Its entry is entry(arg, fiberFrom), on the guest stack it was given (r1 16-byte
aligned, back chain 0). Finalize on a suspended context sets a kill flag; its
host thread longjmps from the suspending call to its base frame and exits, and
Finalize joins it (the jump skips lifted frames and the HLE dispatch frame,
which hold no lock, as a guest longjmp does). Host records are kept for the
next Initialize, because each context's ppu_context joins the runtime's
lwarx/stwcx reservation set (ppu_resv_register), which has no removal.
Process exit with suspended contexts does not wait for them.

Error codes follow RPCS3's argument checks (NULL_POINTER, ALIGN; the calls are
stubs there) and the SDK's meanings: PERM for Run from a context or a
scheduler fiber and for Switch, ReturnToThread or CheckStackLimit from a
thread; INVAL for an address that holds no context; STAT for Run, Switch or
Finalize on a running context, Run or Switch on one whose entry returned (it
has ended, and Run returned cause 0), a Switch to itself, Initialize on a live
context, and CheckStackLimit with r1 outside the context's stack; INVAL for a
guest stack under 1 KB; AGAIN when no host thread can be created. The
execution option and the attribute contents are not used (AttributeInitialize
zeroes the 128-byte attribute, as RPCS3 does). ps3_fiber_context_host_threads()
(not an SDK call) counts the host threads contexts hold. A Run from a host
thread with no PPU context, and a host thread created on the default stack
(the 256 MB reservation refused), are logged once and each time.

Why: titles that drive a coroutine with Run / ReturnToThread (one Run per
frame is a typical pattern) stalled for good on the faked success, since the
work the context does never happened.

Test: tools/test_cellfiber_ppu.py (new) builds libs/spurs/tests/
test_fiber_context.c with cellFiber.c: the entry returning, ReturnToThread and
resume, A->B->A switches keeping each context's registers and guest stack,
Self, thread identity across two owner threads and a host thread with no PPU
context (which gets 0x7FFF0000, not the last owner's id), host thread-locals
starting empty, Finalize of never-run, suspended (in ReturnToThread and in Switch) and
ended contexts with the host threads counted back to zero, every error code
above (Run and Finalize on a running context from another host thread), and
a timed round trip; then runs it with "exit" (contexts left suspended, main
returns) under a 20 s timeout, and runs tests/fiber_switch, whose main.c gains
a ppu_resv_register stub.

diff --git a/libs/spurs/cellFiber.c b/libs/spurs/cellFiber.c
index 3673985c..eb880b72 100644
--- a/libs/spurs/cellFiber.c
+++ b/libs/spurs/cellFiber.c
@@ -8,6 +8,9 @@
  *
  * Not modelled: the scheduler attribute and fiber attribute contents (both are zeroed on initialisation and ignored),
  * and the fiber context-switch trace/ufiber utilities of the SDK.
+ *
+ * The fiber contexts (cellFiberPpuContext*, at the end of this file) do not use ucontext: each context runs on a host
+ * thread of its own, see the comment there.
  */
 
 /* Darwin gates the ucontext routines AND the shape of ucontext_t itself on _XOPEN_SOURCE, so this has to come before
@@ -21,6 +24,7 @@
 #include "cellFiber.h"
 #include "../../runtime/ppu/ppu_memory.h"   /* vm_base, vm_write32, vm_memset: guest EA -> host */
 #include "../../runtime/syscalls/sys_ppu_thread.h"   /* ppu_context, g_ppu_thread_entry_trampoline */
+#include <setjmp.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
@@ -547,3 +551,421 @@ s32 cellFiberPpuJoinFiber(CellFiberPpu* fiber, s32* status)
     UNLOCK();
     return rc;
 }
+
+/* ===========================================================================
+ * Fiber contexts (cellFiberPpuContext*)
+ *
+ * The SDK's low-level fibers: a PPU thread runs a context with cellFiberPpuContextRun, the context runs until it
+ * calls cellFiberPpuContextReturnToThread (Run then returns the cause it passed), and contexts hand control to each
+ * other with cellFiberPpuContextSwitch. On the console a context is a saved register set and a guest stack, and it
+ * runs on the PPU thread that resumed it.
+ *
+ * Lifted, a suspended context also has host frames: the lifted functions it was in the middle of, down to the import
+ * call that suspended it. So every context runs on a host thread of its own, created by Initialize, and a baton
+ * (one lock, a condition variable per context and per Run) lets exactly one of them, or the thread blocked in Run,
+ * execute at a time. A host thread per context, rather than ucontext as the scheduler above uses, keeps every
+ * host thread-local of the runtime per context with no list to keep in step: the guest setjmp chain (a guest longjmp
+ * can only reach a setjmp made on its own context, and a context's chain starts empty), the indirect-call depth, the
+ * tail-call trampoline, the callback stack slot. The handoff costs a few microseconds; titles switch a few times a
+ * frame.
+ *
+ * Guest identity: a context runs on the PPU thread that resumed it, so on every Run or Switch it takes that thread's
+ * thread_id and r13 (TLS). sys_ppu_thread_get_id and __thread data inside a context are the running thread's.
+ *
+ * Finalize on a suspended context wakes its host thread with a kill flag; the thread longjmps from the suspending call
+ * back to its base frame and exits, and Finalize joins it. The longjmp skips the lifted frames and the HLE dispatch
+ * frame of that call, as a guest longjmp does (runtime/ppu/ppu_sjlj.h); none of them holds a lock. The context's host
+ * record (with the ppu_context the reservation set holds) is kept for the next Initialize.
+ *
+ * Choices where the SDK documents nothing and RPCS3 stubs the call: an entry that returns ends the context and returns
+ * to the thread with cause 0, and an ended context cannot be run or switched to again (STAT); Initialize on a live
+ * context is STAT; a guest stack under 1 KB is INVAL; CheckStackLimit is STAT when r1 is outside the context's
+ * stack. The execution option and the attribute (zeroed by AttributeInitialize, as RPCS3 does) are not used. The
+ * argument checks (NULL_POINTER, ALIGN) follow RPCS3.
+ * =========================================================================*/
+
+enum { X_READY, X_RUNNING, X_SUSPENDED, X_ENDED };
+
+#define XCTX_HOST_STACK   (256u * 1024u * 1024u)   /* reserved, as for PPU threads (sys_ppu_thread.c) */
+#define XCTX_MIN_STACK    0x400u
+
+#ifdef _WIN32
+typedef CONDITION_VARIABLE xcond;
+static SRWLOCK s_xlock = SRWLOCK_INIT;
+#  define XLOCK()        AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&s_xlock)
+#  define XUNLOCK()      ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&s_xlock)
+#  define XCINIT(c)      InitializeConditionVariable(c)
+#  define XCDESTROY(c)   ((void)(c))
+#  define XWAIT(c)       SleepConditionVariableSRW((c), &s_xlock, INFINITE, 0)
+#  define XWAKE(c)       WakeAllConditionVariable(c)
+typedef HANDLE xthread;
+#else
+typedef pthread_cond_t xcond;
+static pthread_mutex_t s_xlock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+#  define XLOCK()        pthread_mutex_lock(&s_xlock)
+#  define XUNLOCK()      pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_xlock)
+#  define XCINIT(c)      pthread_cond_init((c), NULL)
+#  define XCDESTROY(c)   pthread_cond_destroy(c)
+#  define XWAIT(c)       pthread_cond_wait((c), &s_xlock)
+#  define XWAKE(c)       pthread_cond_broadcast(c)
+typedef pthread_t xthread;
+#endif
+
+/* One cellFiberPpuContextRun in progress, on the stack of the thread that called it. */
+typedef struct {
+    int   done;
+    s32   cause;
+    u32   from;                  /* the context that returned to the thread */
+    xcond cv;
+} XRun;
+
+typedef struct XCtx XCtx;
+struct XCtx {
+    XCtx*   next;                /* live list, or the free list once finalized */
+    u32     ea;                  /* the guest CellFiberPpuContext */
+    u32     opd;
+    u32     stack_ea;
+    u32     stack_size;
+    int     state;
+    int     go;                  /* the baton: this context may run */
+    int     kill;                /* Finalize: unwind and exit */
+    int     exited;              /* the host thread has left its body */
+    int     registered;          /* ctx is in the runtime's reservation set */
+    u32     from;                /* who resumed it last: a context, or 0 for a thread */
+    XRun*   run;                 /* the Run it executes for, while RUNNING */
+    xcond   cv;
+    xthread thread;
+    jmp_buf unwind;
+    ppu_context ctx;
+};
+
+static XCtx* s_xlive;
+static XCtx* s_xfree;
+static int   s_xthreads;         /* host threads that have not left their body */
+static PPU_THREAD_LOCAL XCtx* t_xcur;
+
+/* The runtime's lwarx/stwcx reservation set (ppu_loader.cpp): every context's ppu_context joins it, once per host
+ * record, so a store by another thread breaks a reservation the context holds. */
+extern void ppu_resv_register(ppu_context* c);
+
+static XCtx* find_xctx(u32 ea)   /* the lock is held */
+{
+    for (XCtx* c = s_xlive; c; c = c->next)
+        if (c->ea == ea) return c;
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+/* Gives the baton to `c` for `run`, resumed by `from` (0: a thread) on the PPU thread `owner`. The lock is held. */
+static void xctx_resume_locked(XCtx* c, XRun* run, u32 from, const ppu_context* owner)
+{
+    c->run  = run;
+    c->from = from;
+    if (owner) {
+        c->ctx.gpr[13]   = owner->gpr[13];
+        c->ctx.thread_id = owner->thread_id;
+    } else {
+        /* Resumed by a host thread with no guest context: it gets no stale identity of an earlier owner. */
+        static int s_warned = 0;
+        if (!s_warned) {
+            s_warned = 1;
+            fprintf(stderr, "[cellFiber] context 0x%08X resumed with no PPU thread context; thread_id 0x%llX\n",
+                    c->ea, (unsigned long long)FIBER_FALLBACK_THREAD_ID);
+        }
+        c->ctx.gpr[13]   = 0;
+        c->ctx.thread_id = FIBER_FALLBACK_THREAD_ID;
+    }
+    c->state = X_RUNNING;
+    c->go    = 1;
+    XWAKE(&c->cv);
+}
+
+/* `c` ends its turn: the thread blocked in Run gets `cause` back. The lock is held. */
+static void xctx_return_locked(XCtx* c, s32 cause)
+{
+    XRun* r = c->run;
+    c->run = NULL;
+    if (!r) return;
+    r->cause = cause;
+    r->from  = c->ea;
+    r->done  = 1;
+    XWAKE(&r->cv);
+}
+
+/* The calling context waits for the baton. The lock is held, and is held again on return; a Finalize meanwhile
+ * unwinds the host thread instead (the lock is released first). */
+static void xctx_suspend_locked(XCtx* c)
+{
+    while (!c->go && !c->kill) XWAIT(&c->cv);
+    if (c->kill) {
+        XUNLOCK();
+        longjmp(c->unwind, 1);
+    }
+    c->go = 0;
+}
+
+#ifdef _WIN32
+static DWORD WINAPI xctx_thread(LPVOID p)
+#else
+static void* xctx_thread(void* p)
+#endif
+{
+    XCtx* c = (XCtx*)p;
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+    pthread_setname_np("ppu fiber context");
+#endif
+    t_xcur       = c;
+    g_active_ctx = &c->ctx;
+
+    XLOCK();
+    while (!c->go && !c->kill) XWAIT(&c->cv);
+    const int killed = c->kill;
+    c->go = 0;
+    XUNLOCK();
+
+    if (!killed && setjmp(c->unwind) == 0) {
+        c->ctx.gpr[4] = c->from;                  /* entry(arg, fiberFrom) */
+        if (g_ppu_thread_entry_trampoline)
+            g_ppu_thread_entry_trampoline(&c->ctx);
+        XLOCK();
+        c->state = X_ENDED;                       /* the entry returned */
+        xctx_return_locked(c, 0);
+        XUNLOCK();
+    }
+
+    XLOCK();
+    c->exited = 1;
+    s_xthreads--;
+    XWAKE(&c->cv);
+    XUNLOCK();
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    return 0;
+#else
+    return NULL;
+#endif
+}
+
+static int xctx_start_thread(XCtx* c)
+{
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    c->thread = CreateThread(NULL, XCTX_HOST_STACK, xctx_thread, c, STACK_SIZE_PARAM_IS_A_RESERVATION, NULL);
+    return c->thread != NULL;
+#else
+    pthread_attr_t attr;
+    pthread_attr_init(&attr);
+    pthread_attr_setstacksize(&attr, XCTX_HOST_STACK);
+    int rc = pthread_create(&c->thread, &attr, xctx_thread, c);
+    if (rc) {
+        /* The default stack, rather than nothing; a deep lifted call chain may then overflow it. */
+        fprintf(stderr, "[cellFiber] context 0x%08X: no %u MB host stack (error %d); using the default stack\n",
+                c->ea, XCTX_HOST_STACK >> 20, rc);
+        rc = pthread_create(&c->thread, NULL, xctx_thread, c);
+    }
+    pthread_attr_destroy(&attr);
+    return rc == 0;
+#endif
+}
+
+static void xctx_join_thread(XCtx* c)
+{
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    WaitForSingleObject(c->thread, INFINITE);
+    CloseHandle(c->thread);
+#else
+    pthread_join(c->thread, NULL);
+#endif
+}
+
+int ps3_fiber_context_host_threads(void)
+{
+    XLOCK();
+    const int n = s_xthreads;
+    XUNLOCK();
+    return n;
+}
+
+s32 _cellFiberPpuContextAttributeInitialize(CellFiberPpuContextAttribute* attr, u32 sdkVersion)
+{
+    (void)sdkVersion;
+    const u32 ea = (u32)(uintptr_t)attr;
+    if (!ea) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_NULL_POINTER;
+    if (ea % CELL_FIBER_PPU_CONTEXT_ATTRIBUTE_ALIGN) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_ALIGN;
+    vm_memset(ea, 0, CELL_FIBER_PPU_CONTEXT_ATTRIBUTE_SIZE);   /* debuggerSupport false */
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
+
+s32 cellFiberPpuContextInitialize(CellFiberPpuContext* context, u32 entry, u64 arg, void* eaStack, u32 sizeStack,
+                                  const CellFiberPpuContextAttribute* attr)
+{
+    (void)attr;
+    const u32 ea       = (u32)(uintptr_t)context;
+    const u32 stack_ea = (u32)(uintptr_t)eaStack;
+    if (!ea || !entry || !stack_ea) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_NULL_POINTER;
+    if (ea % CELL_FIBER_PPU_CONTEXT_ALIGN) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_ALIGN;
+    if (sizeStack < XCTX_MIN_STACK) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_INVAL;
+
+    XLOCK();
+    if (find_xctx(ea)) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_STAT; }
+    XCtx* c = s_xfree;
+    if (c) {
+        s_xfree = c->next;
+    } else {
+        c = (XCtx*)calloc(1, sizeof *c);
+        if (!c) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_NOMEM; }
+        XCINIT(&c->cv);
+    }
+    /* A reused record keeps its condition variable (it is never copied) and its place in the reservation set. */
+    c->next       = NULL;
+    c->go         = 0;
+    c->kill       = 0;
+    c->exited     = 0;
+    c->from       = 0;
+    c->run        = NULL;
+    memset(&c->thread, 0, sizeof c->thread);
+    memset(&c->unwind, 0, sizeof c->unwind);
+    memset(&c->ctx, 0, sizeof c->ctx);
+    c->ea         = ea;
+    c->opd        = entry;
+    c->stack_ea   = stack_ea;
+    c->stack_size = sizeStack;
+    c->state      = X_READY;
+
+    /* The initialising thread's identity and FP state until a Run hands it the running thread's. */
+    const ppu_context* me = g_active_ctx;
+    c->ctx.gpr[1]    = (stack_ea + sizeStack - FIBER_STACK_TOP_PAD) & ~0xFull;
+    c->ctx.gpr[3]    = arg;
+    c->ctx.gpr[13]   = me ? me->gpr[13] : 0;
+    c->ctx.thread_id = me ? me->thread_id : FIBER_FALLBACK_THREAD_ID;
+    c->ctx.fpscr     = me ? me->fpscr : 0;
+    c->ctx.vscr      = me ? me->vscr : PPU_VSCR_NJ;
+    c->ctx.cia       = entry;
+    vm_write64((u32)c->ctx.gpr[1], 0);          /* the back chain ends here */
+
+    /* Joins the reservation set before its host thread can run it (ppu_resv_register takes no lock). */
+    if (!c->registered) {
+        c->registered = 1;
+        ppu_resv_register(&c->ctx);
+    }
+    if (!xctx_start_thread(c)) {
+        c->next = s_xfree;
+        s_xfree = c;
+        XUNLOCK();
+        return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_AGAIN;
+    }
+    s_xthreads++;
+    c->next = s_xlive;
+    s_xlive = c;
+    XUNLOCK();
+
+    static int s_logged = 0;
+    if (s_logged < 8) {
+        s_logged++;
+        fprintf(stderr, "[cellFiber] context 0x%08X: entry=0x%08X arg=0x%llX stack=0x%08X+0x%X\n",
+                ea, entry, (unsigned long long)arg, stack_ea, sizeStack);
+    }
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
+
+s32 cellFiberPpuContextFinalize(CellFiberPpuContext* context)
+{
+    const u32 ea = (u32)(uintptr_t)context;
+    if (!ea) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_NULL_POINTER;
+    if (ea % CELL_FIBER_PPU_CONTEXT_ALIGN) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_ALIGN;
+
+    XLOCK();
+    XCtx* c = find_xctx(ea);
+    if (!c) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_INVAL; }
+    if (c->state == X_RUNNING) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_STAT; }
+    for (XCtx** pc = &s_xlive; *pc; pc = &(*pc)->next)
+        if (*pc == c) { *pc = c->next; break; }
+    c->kill = 1;
+    XWAKE(&c->cv);
+    while (!c->exited) XWAIT(&c->cv);
+    XUNLOCK();
+
+    xctx_join_thread(c);
+
+    XLOCK();
+    c->next = s_xfree;
+    s_xfree = c;
+    XUNLOCK();
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
+
+s32 cellFiberPpuContextRun(CellFiberPpuContext* context, s32* cause, CellFiberPpuContext** fiberFrom,
+                           const CellFiberPpuContextExecutionOption* option)
+{
+    (void)option;
+    const u32 ea = (u32)(uintptr_t)context;
+    if (!ea || !cause) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_NULL_POINTER;
+    if (ea % CELL_FIBER_PPU_CONTEXT_ALIGN) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_ALIGN;
+    if (t_xcur || t_cur) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_PERM;    /* threads only */
+
+    XLOCK();
+    XCtx* c = find_xctx(ea);
+    if (!c) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_INVAL; }
+    if (c->state == X_RUNNING || c->state == X_ENDED) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_STAT; }
+    XRun r;
+    memset(&r, 0, sizeof r);
+    XCINIT(&r.cv);
+    xctx_resume_locked(c, &r, 0, g_active_ctx);
+    while (!r.done) XWAIT(&r.cv);
+    XUNLOCK();
+    XCDESTROY(&r.cv);
+
+    vm_write32((u32)(uintptr_t)cause, (u32)r.cause);
+    if (fiberFrom) vm_write32((u32)(uintptr_t)fiberFrom, r.from);
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
+
+s32 cellFiberPpuContextSwitch(CellFiberPpuContext* context, CellFiberPpuContext** fiberFrom,
+                              const CellFiberPpuContextExecutionOption* option)
+{
+    (void)option;
+    XCtx* me = t_xcur;
+    if (!me) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_PERM;
+    const u32 ea = (u32)(uintptr_t)context;
+    if (!ea) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_NULL_POINTER;
+    if (ea % CELL_FIBER_PPU_CONTEXT_ALIGN) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_ALIGN;
+
+    XLOCK();
+    XCtx* to = find_xctx(ea);
+    if (!to) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_INVAL; }
+    if (to == me || to->state == X_RUNNING || to->state == X_ENDED) { XUNLOCK(); return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_STAT; }
+    XRun* run = me->run;
+    me->run   = NULL;
+    me->state = X_SUSPENDED;
+    xctx_resume_locked(to, run, me->ea, &me->ctx);
+    xctx_suspend_locked(me);
+    const u32 from = me->from;
+    XUNLOCK();
+
+    if (fiberFrom) vm_write32((u32)(uintptr_t)fiberFrom, from);
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
+
+s32 cellFiberPpuContextReturnToThread(s32 cause)
+{
+    XCtx* me = t_xcur;
+    if (!me) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_PERM;
+    XLOCK();
+    me->state = X_SUSPENDED;
+    xctx_return_locked(me, cause);
+    xctx_suspend_locked(me);
+    XUNLOCK();
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
+
+s32 cellFiberPpuContextCheckStackLimit(void)
+{
+    const XCtx* me = t_xcur;
+    if (!me) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_PERM;
+    const u64 sp = me->ctx.gpr[1];
+    if (sp < me->stack_ea || sp > (u64)me->stack_ea + me->stack_size) return (s32)CELL_FIBER_ERROR_STAT;
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
+
+CellFiberPpuContext* cellFiberPpuContextSelf(void)
+{
+    const XCtx* me = t_xcur;
+    return (CellFiberPpuContext*)(uintptr_t)(me ? me->ea : 0);
+}
diff --git a/libs/spurs/cellFiber.h b/libs/spurs/cellFiber.h
index be88d447..093d4308 100644
--- a/libs/spurs/cellFiber.h
+++ b/libs/spurs/cellFiber.h
@@ -8,6 +8,11 @@
  * JoinFiber. Each fiber has its own guest stack (the caller's eaStack) and its
